{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgsyPFefAPVMuyz77RGyTG","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-ejwur28f\ntotal 16\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff      128 Nov 21 13:23 .\ndrwx------@ 33232 brenn  staff  1063424 Nov 21 13:23 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    14 brenn  staff      448 Oct  2 03:50 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff     5065 Nov 21 13:23 sheet.md\n# Independent coverage discovery: E08 — Bounded delegated authority\n\nEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\nreview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n**Requirement:** Give sub-agents only the powers approved for their task. Preserve the verified original subject and current actor through each handoff and enforce their task, tenant, resource, and audience limits where the action runs. Use supported token exchange or narrow task credentials rather than copying a parent's full credential. A parent must not gain a denied power by asking a more powerful peer to act without separate valid approval. For RFC 8693 tokens, earlier nested actors are provenance only and never add access. An actor chain or signed identity does not prove that a requested action was approved. Test legitimate delegation and that escalation attempt.\n**N/A condition:** The agent never delegates to sub-agents or peer agents.\n\nInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\nhandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\nunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\nomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\ninput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\nSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\ncoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\nby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\njust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n\nSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\nsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\nverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\notherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n\n\n## E08.1\n\n**Check:** Each child gets a credential narrowed to its approved task (for example by token exchange or transaction tokens), never the parent's full credential.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find where a child agent gets its credential. 2) Check it is a narrowed token for the task (token exchange, transaction token, scoped-down role). 3) Answer no if any spawn path passes the parent's token, API key, or full role, or the child inherits the parent's environment credentials.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E08.2\n\n**Check:** Authorization at the action uses the original subject and the current actor, and earlier actors in the delegation chain never add access.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open authorization code for delegated actions. 2) Check it decides on the original subject and the current actor. 3) Answer no if it grants access because of any earlier actor in the chain (nested `act` claims, parent identity) or a union of chain permissions.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E08.3\n\n**Check:** An action the parent was denied is also denied when routed through a more powerful peer, unless it carries its own explicit approval.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find how a parent asks a peer or child to act. 2) Check the request carries the parent's limits and the peer re-checks them, or requires its own explicit approval. 3) Answer no if a peer acts with its own wider permissions on a parent's request without that check.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## E08.4\n\n**Check:** Downstream services reject the parent's token when the child presents it (audience-bound tokens).\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find how child tokens are issued and how downstream services validate tokens. 2) Check tokens are audience-bound and services verify `aud`. 3) Answer no if audience is unset, a wildcard, or not checked. Answer unknown if downstream services are outside this repo.\n\n**Coverage policy:** {}\n\n**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to E08.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"E08\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"E08.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\nagent\nagent/migrations\nagent/migrations/001_init.sql\nagent/requirements.txt\nagent/config\nagent/config/agent.yaml\nagent/config/tools.yaml\nagent/Dockerfile\nagent/k8s\nagent/k8s/deployment.yaml\nagent/k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml\nagent/k8s/admission.yaml\nagent/k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\nagent/CODEOWNERS\nagent/.mcp.json\nagent/release\nagent/rel